# TODO / Roadmap

**Goal:** Make the core pipeline robust and modular.

- [x] Refactor core pipeline:
  - [x] Separate internal functions:
    - [x] `convert_to_pdf(input, output)`
    - [x] `add_watermark(pdf_file, options)`
    - [x] `encrypt_pdf(pdf_file, options)`
- [x] Make CLI mirror the same pipeline (single command + optional modular use).
- [x] Add LibreOffice headless mode handling:
  - [x] Automatically start/stop LibreOffice service when needed
  - [x] Detect and handle LibreOffice runtime errors gracefully
- [x] Add clear README examples for:
  - [x] Converting Word, LibreOffice, and image files to PDF
  - [x] Applying watermarks to PDFs
  - [x] Encrypting PDFs with user/owner passwords
- [x] Update README with dependency list:
  - [x] PoDoFo (PDF processing)
  - [x] CLI11 (command-line interface)
  - [x] LibreOffice (document conversion, headless mode)
- [ ] Stabilize core pipeline and test against crashes
  - [ ] Ensure LibreOffice runtime is robust and cleanly shuts down
- [x] Document and implement all LibreOffice conversions to PDF
  - [x] List all document types LibreOffice can convert (doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, odt, ods, odp, rtf, txt, etc.)
  - [ ] Map each input file type to PDF conversion using soffice
  - [ ] Include MIME types for each document type for automatic converter selection
- [x] List all image types supported by ImageMagick (jpg, jpeg, png, gif, tiff, bmp, etc.)
  - [ ] Map each image MIME type to PDF conversion
- [ ] Enhance converter selection logic
  - [ ] Use MIME type mapping to automatically select the appropriate converter (LibreOffice vs ImageMagick)
  - [ ] Gracefully handle unsupported file types with clear error messages
- [ ] Outcome: Stable and flexible foundation ready for first release

**Goal:** Add lightweight PDF operations inspired by Antenna House.

- [ ] Implement PDF merging (combine multiple PDFs).
- [ ] Implement page extraction and reordering.
- [ ] Add optional PDF flattening for reliable watermarks/encryption.
- [ ] Outcome: Library becomes a true multi-step PDF tool.

**Goal:** Improve watermark/encryption features.

### Watermarking
- [ ] Add positioning options (top, center, bottom, margins, tiling).
- [ ] Support rotation, opacity, and font styles.
- [ ] Add image watermark support (size, position, transparency).

### Encryption
- [ ] Support multiple algorithms (AES128, AES256).
- [ ] Implement granular permissions (print, edit, copy, fill, annotate).
- [ ] Separate handling of owner/user passwords.
- [ ] Outcome: Strong security and branding capabilities.


**Goal:** Advance features.

- [ ] Implement text extraction for indexing/search.
- [ ] Add optional PDF/A compliance conversion.
- [ ] Extend CLI flexibility:
  - [ ] Add modular flags: `--convert`, `--watermark`, `--encrypt`.
  - [ ] Allow skipping steps dynamically.
- [ ] Add batch processing (directories of files).
- [ ] Outcome: Versatile PDF automation pipeline.

## Optional Stretch Goals
- [ ] Output format conversions: PDF → SVG, XPS, Word.
- [ ] Internationalization (Unicode/CJK font support in watermarking).
- [ ] Integration examples:
  - [ ] Python bindings.
  - [ ] Docker-based CLI image.
